 ## Shared principles
-The core mechanism is the evaluation of the volume rendering equation and the propagation of gradients through the integration steps [G]. The standard emission-absorption model computes the color $\hat{C}(\mathbf{r})$ for a ray $\mathbf{r}$ as [S1, unofficial]:
+The core mechanism is the evaluation of the volume rendering equation and the propagation of gradients through the integration steps [G]. The standard emission-absorption model computes the color $\hat{C}(\mathbf{r})$ for a ray $\mathbf{r}$ as [G]:
 
 $$
-\hat{C}(\mathbf{r}) = \sum_{i=1}^N T_i (1 - \exp(-\sigma_i \delta_i)) \mathbf{c}_i
+\hat{C}(\mathbf{r}) = \sum_{i=1}^N T_i (1 - \exp(-\kappa_i \delta_i)) \mathbf{c}_i
